 this reference card, a letter to Prince Morkin from Rothron the Wise, the Lords of Midnight chronicles and your CD-ROM. If any of these items are missing, please consult with your software dealer.\par \par }\pard\plain \s1\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f4\lang2057\cgrid {Installation and loading Instructions\par }\pard\plain \widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\uldb\lang2057\cgrid {\b\ulnone \par CD-ROM\par }{\ulnone To enter the realms of the Blood March you need to first install & then load the game. To install the game, insert the CD-ROM into your CD-ROM drive on your PC. Now log onto the drive as usual. For example, if your CD-ROM is designated as Drive E, type E: then press Enter. At the DOS prompt, type INSTALL then press Enter. Now follow the on-screen instructions. When installation is complete you will be returned to DOS. To run the game, type MIDNIGHT and then press Enter.\par \par }{\b\ulnone Control devices\par }\pard\plain \s15\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\lang2057\cgrid {To use a mouse you need to have a Microsoft compatible mouse driver installed. If you run the game without a mouse driver, the game will assume joystick control. Throughout the main manual, mouse control is assumed. Joystick control is identical, except you are expected to use fire button 1 for the left mouse button, and fire button two [sic] for the right.\par }\pard\plain \widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\uldb\lang2057\cgrid {\ulnone \par }{\b\ulnone Save game files}{\ulnone \par Whenever the game is saved, either automatically every Midnight or by you, the save game files are placed in a directory named after the colour of the current book. For example, the Black book of the Blood March will be saved into a directory named BLACK which is contained within the directory that the Citadel was installed to on your hard disk.\par For any last minute changes please check for the presence of a READ.ME ascii text file on your CD-ROM. If there is no file, then all the requirements stated here are accurate at the time of publication.\par \par }\pard \qc\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\ulnone \page }{\b\ulnone Dramatis Personae\par }\pard \widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\ulnone \par [BOROTH\rquote S PORTRAIT]\par Boroth the Wolfheart, High King of the Marish, King of the Dark Fey, steeped in centuries [sic] evil and bloodlust, who seeks to enslave all the realms of the Bloodmarch [sic] and the fair land of Midnight itself. The one who must be destroyed to save all.\par \par [LUXOR\rquote S PORTRAIT]\par Luxor the Moonprince, Prince of Midnight, Lord of Xajorkith Prince of the Free, victor of the War of the Solstice against Doomdark and the war of the Icemark against Doomdark\rquote s daughter, Shareth the Heartstealer. Luxor is being held to ransom by Boroth the Wolfheart in the dark Citadel of Maranor. Captured by Boroth following his shipwreck on the coast of the Marish during a voyage to Coromand in search of the magical jewel, the Eye of the Moon. Father of Prince Morkin and grandfather of Corleth of Corelay and, unbeknownst to him, Anderlane of the Arakai.\par \par [MORKIN\rquote S PORTRAIT]\par Prince Morkin, Lord of Corelay, Son of Luxor the Moonprince and husband of Tarithel the Fey, daughter of the Lord of Dreams, who has been given charge of Midnight during Luxor\rquote s voyage to Coromand south beyond the Blood March. It has fallen upon Morkin to set forth into the Blood March to rescue his father from Boroth\rquote s clutches and to destroy the Wolfheart: Morkin is the father of Corleth of Corelay and, unbeknownst to him, Anderlane of the Arakai.\par \par [ARALETH\rquote S PORTRAIT]\par Araleth the White, Lord of Dreams, Father of Tarithel the Fey and thus father-in-law of Prince Morkin, Araleth played a key part in both the War of the Solstice and the War of the Icemark and now stands ready at Morkin\rquote s side to do battle against Boroth the Wolfheart and his Dark Fey hordes.\par \par \page [ROTHRON\rquote S PORTRAIT]\par Rorthron the Wise, Guardian of the Tower of the Moon, One of the Wise, an ancient race of deep powers and knowledge, Rorthron has given counsel to Luxor in both the War of the Solstice and the War of the Icemark. Now, he is already deep within the Blood March heading for the Last Northing and the Crimson Mountains, having learnt that Prince Morkin has not just one son, Corleth of Corelay but a second son, Andelane of the Arakai, born out of wedlock, issue of Morkin and Shareth the Heartstealer but raised and nurtured in the Blood March by his surrogate mother, Cirithel of the Crimson Mountains. Rorthron suspects that Anderlane can offer invaluable help in the coming war against Boroth.\par \par [CORLETH\rquote S PORTRAIT]\par Corleth of Corelay, Lord of Thimrath Son of Prince Morkin and Princess Tarithel, grandson of Luxor the Moonprince and half-brother of Anderlane of the Arakai, Corleth had been accompanying his grandfather on the voyage to Coromand together with his friend, Arin. When they were captured by Boroth and taken to the Dark Citadel of Maranor, Luxor secured the release of the two boys by passing them off as servants. Now, however, Corleth and Arin have double-backed to the Citadel and, after finding a hidden entrance, they are at loose in the dungeons seeking to find and rescue Luxor.\par \par [ARIN\rquote S PORTRAIT]\par Arin Lord Blood, Lord of Valethor Son of the Lord Blood who stood side-by-side with Luxor against Doomdark\rquote s hordes during the War of the Solstice, Arin was accompanying his father on Luxor\rquote s voyage to Coromand. After the shipwreck, his father Lord Blood was slain defending the unconscious Moonprince and Arin, now the new Lord Blood was taken prisoner together with his friend Corleth and the Moonprince. Now, with Corleth, he is armed and at large in the dungeons of Maranor, seeking to rescue Luxor.\par \par [ANDERLANE\rquote S PORTRAIT]\par Anderlane of the Arakai, Lord of the Crimson Mountains unsuspected grandson of Luxor the Moonprince, half-brother of Corleth of Corelay and son of Prince Morkin and Shareth the Heartstealer, Anderlane was conceived during the War of the Icemark whilst Morkin lay helpless under Shareth\rquote s enchantments and, by Shareth\rquote s magic, was born to a surrogate mother, Cirithel of the Crimson Mountains. There, in the Last Northing in the east of the Blood March, Anderlane was raised as though he were Cirithel\rquote s own son. As yet, he knows nothing of his true origins but Rorthron suspects that he will play a key role in the coming war.\par \par }\pard \qc\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\ulnone \page }{\b\ulnone Keyboard Summary\par }\pard \widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\ulnone \par }{\b\ulnone Whilst controlling a character...\par }\pard\plain \s15\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\lang2057\cgrid {f1\tab Talk to someone (when facing someone)\par f2\tab Attack someone (when facing someone)\par f3\tab Attack a stronghold (when near building)\par f4\tab Enter a building (when near building)\par }\pard\plain \widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\uldb\lang2057\cgrid {\ulnone f5\tab Mount or dismount a dragon (when near or riding a dragon)\par f6\tab Board a ship or go ashore (when near or on-board a boat)\par f7\tab Swap/Pickup a weapon (when facing a person or weapon)\par f10\tab Initiate Rescue (when facing a hostage)\par Tab\tab Interior combat against Trolls\par \par }{\b\ulnone When controlling or watching a character...\par }\pard\plain \s15\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\lang2057\cgrid {Esc Halt\tab Direct control/watching mode (also has the effect of pausing the game)\par }\pard\plain \widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\uldb\lang2057\cgrid {\ulnone 1-6\tab Change camera views (outdoors only)\par 0\tab Fix camera position for \lquote fly by\rquote  effect (outdoors only)\par Num + and -\tab Increase/decrease brightness level for dark monitors (indoors only)\par \tab Increase/decrease graphic level (outdoors only)\par Num *\tab Turns in-game music on/off\par \par }{\b\ulnone Whilst time is racing on...\par }{\ulnone Esc\tab Stop time racing on\par \par }{\b\ulnone PC CD-ROM BONUS\par }\pard\plain \s15\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\lang2057\cgrid {You will find a couple of bonus programs included on the CD-ROM. They are PC conversions of the original 8-bit Sinclair ZX Spectrum prequels \ldblquote The Lords of Midnight\rdblquote  and \ldblquote Doomdark\rquote s Revenge\rdblquote . Read the ascii files MIDNIGHT.TXT and REVENGE.TXT on the CD-ROM for further instructions.\par }\pard\plain \widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f4\uldb\lang2057\cgrid {\ulnone \par }{\b\ulnone PROBLEMS}{\ulnone \par If you experience any problems whilst trying to install or run The Citadel, please contact the customer help-line located in the back of your game manual.\par \par \par  \par \par [END OF REFERENCE CARD]\par \par \par \par }}